{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853179-making-a-3e-lunar-could-use-some-help","id":853179,"title":"Making a 3e Lunar, could use some help.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-25T14:59:31-07:00","id":853179,"title":"Making a 3e Lunar, could use some help.","content":"So I am playing an Eclipse caste loosely modeled after Itami from GATE:<br /> <br /> More specifically, an ex-wyld hunt officer who escaped when he decided that sacrificing a city of 200,000 people was too big a loss for one solar. (Thanks, Deled. You jerk.)<br /> <br /> However, we passed through an area known for being populated by a few lunars. And my Storyteller told me that in the near future a particular lunar would be coming near our circle to investigate, because our prior exaltations were comrades and her memories are spurring her to check me out.<br /> <br /> My storyteller, however, assigned me to deciding what kind of lunar she is, etc. There isn't any kinds of required relationship dynamic, but if she's supposed to be at the least a useful ally.<br /> <br /> I am trying to start a discussion where I can bounce around ideas for building a lunar ally. I'd like to pick an uncommon totem, but I'm not sure what to pick. Maybe something like a frog, or raven?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T16:44:13-07:00","id":853228,"title":"","content":"...Brain, no, shut up, Rory is creepy and made of Police Watchlist This Author flags tied up in a bunch of frilly ribbons. Even if she is the ultimate posterchild for a Grand Grimcleaver wielder.<br /> <br /> Um. Uncommon choices of animal... Lemme see... Slug. Cone shell. Snapping turtle. Yeddim. Beetle - take your pick what kind, there's an infinite variety. Parrot. Praying mantis (Dammit, brain, I said<i> not</i> Rory). Stick insect. Roadrunner. Termite. Shrike. Frilled lizard.<br /> <br /> ...Those are the ones that jump to mind for brainstorming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T19:37:03-07:00","id":853284,"title":"","content":"Bird of paradise, peacock, pig, jellyfish, anglerfish, pangolin, anteater, flying snake (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HMs8Cu8PNKM\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Chrysopelea</i></a> okay it's gliding not flying, but still), those hallucinogenic blue-and-red frogs, pygmy marmoset, genetically mutated 3-headed cobra, 9-tailed mole hound, Chiarochuro glass snake, kabuto beetle, mewtwo, tapeworm, giant bat-eating cave millipede that looks like Koh the Face-Stealer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T19:42:28-07:00","id":853286,"title":"","content":"Winged snake that spits acidic venom. Spider, for that ever cool Drider look. Fox for recon. Bat, for the cool gargoyle look","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T19:45:45-07:00","id":853287,"title":"","content":"Frog totem - an ugly witch-girl alchemist (it makes a change from the normal bikini witches) who is a master of poison-making and hallucinogens.<br /> <br /> Raven - a Northern warrior, valkeyrie-esque, one-eyed, but also a loremaster.<br /> <br /> Black dog - Indian, Graeco-Roman or Celtic-themed protector of the dead, uses necromancy to keep the dead where they belong<br /> <br /> Hedgehog - prickly but cute<br /> <br /> Salamander - pyromancer (Ifrit Lord pact sorceress) with regeneration and poison charms<br /> <br /> Cuckoo - spy or undercover agent<br /> <br /> Shrike - a butcher. I mean, literally that was her job before she exalted. Brutal, makes art of her enemies' entrails (perhaps she pushes people away because of issues?)<br /> <br /> Snake - a (No Moon) doctor. Who also uses snake style, obviously (which saves the ST having to work out how to do her combat charms).<br /> <br /> Cat - stealthy burglar. Loves the finer things in life, luxury, jewels, etc. If it's a black cat, also a sorceress.<br /> <br /> Pig - fat but friendly. Very intelligent.<br /> <br /> Goat - You can do a satanic wizard vibe with this, with goat horns or hooves as the tell. But I feel it works better for men than women (beard, randy old goat)<br /> <br /> Otter - crafter (of mundane stuff, not artefacts, because Lunars aren't that great at crafting compared to Solars)<br /> <br /> Octopus - Cthulu-girl! Mad prophet sorceress.<br /> <br /> Shark - berzerker warrior<br /> <br /> Monkey - mischeivous prankster<br /> <br /> Vampire bat - basically, everything you associate with Dracula except being undead. Charming but creepy northern aristocrat.<br /> <br /> Is there something the group is bad at, that isn't combat? That it'd be useful to have someone who's good at it?<br /> (I say not combat, because frankly, having extra NPCs to help the team in combat is kind of annoying for the ST, easier just to have lower-powered encounters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-25-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:16:47-07:00","id":853550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853179-making-a-3e-lunar-could-use-some-help?p=853228#post853228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Brain, no, shut up, Rory is creepy and made of Police Watchlist This Author flags tied up in a bunch of frilly ribbons. Even if she is the ultimate posterchild for a Grand Grimcleaver wielder.<br /> <br /> Um. Uncommon choices of animal... Lemme see... Slug. Cone shell. Snapping turtle. Yeddim. Beetle - take your pick what kind, there's an infinite variety. Parrot. Praying mantis (Dammit, brain, I said<i> not</i> Rory). Stick insect. Roadrunner. Termite. Shrike. Frilled lizard.<br /> <br /> ...Those are the ones that jump to mind for brainstorming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, gonna try to stay away from Jailbat-Prime. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Multiple suggestions for pig... Not against that. Would they be good at survival? I know some farmers use them for finding truffles and stuff. Boar would be too common, huh?<br /> <br /> Ooh! Javelinas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T11:08:43-07:00","id":853580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rungok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853179-making-a-3e-lunar-could-use-some-help?p=853550#post853550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple suggestions for pig... Not against that. Would they be good at survival? I know some farmers use them for finding truffles and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can eat almost anything, they have an extremely good sense of smell, they're really intelligent and trainable (if not a little goofy-looking) - e.g. they can be taught how to use a computer mouse.<br /> <br /> imo they'd be best represented by high Stamina, Intelligence and good Perception. They're not as sociable as people tend to think they are though, being pretty independant (compared to, say, dogs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Boar would be too common, huh?<br /> Ooh! Javelinas? </div> </div> </div>What kind of environment are you looking for? North, East, South or West? Scavanger Lands? River Provinces?<br /> Javelinas are awesome and do well in winter environments, for example, and imo a Lunar is more likely to have a totem that's at least semi-native to their home turf, considering how it's much easier to feel kinship with an animal you've actually heard of (but that may be just me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:02:23-07:00","id":853635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853179-making-a-3e-lunar-could-use-some-help?p=853580#post853580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can eat almost anything, they have an extremely good sense of smell, they're really intelligent and trainable (if not a little goofy-looking) - e.g. they can be taught how to use a computer mouse.<br /> <br /> imo they'd be best represented by high Stamina, Intelligence and good Perception. They're not as sociable as people tend to think they are though, being pretty independant (compared to, say, dogs).<br /> <br /> <br /> What kind of environment are you looking for? North, East, South or West? Scavanger Lands? River Provinces?<br /> Javelinas are awesome and do well in winter environments, for example, and imo a Lunar is more likely to have a totem that's at least semi-native to their home turf, considering how it's much easier to feel kinship with an animal you've actually heard of (but that may be just me).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the north-east area of creation, so javelina is looking good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:10:18-07:00","id":853643,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna say that Fruit Bats are quite cute and doing a Flying Fox instead of a Vampire Bat would be reasonably unusual.<br /> <br /> Less common....hmmmm.... Kangaroo Rat? Kangaroo? Koala? Maybe she's originally from the Caul.<br /> <br /> Alternately, use one of the scary animals in the back of the book, like the Emperor Sloth, Siege Lizard, Ox-Dragon, or Hellboar. Then, you can just have her fight in that shape, using the stats for that animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:37:19-07:00","id":853882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853179-making-a-3e-lunar-could-use-some-help?p=853228#post853228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Brain, no, shut up, Rory is creepy and made of Police Watchlist This Author flags tied up in a bunch of frilly ribbons. Even if she is the ultimate posterchild for a Grand Grimcleaver wielder.<br /> <br /> Um. Uncommon choices of animal... Lemme see... Slug. Cone shell. Snapping turtle. Yeddim. Beetle - take your pick what kind, there's an infinite variety. Parrot. Praying mantis (Dammit, brain, I said<i> not</i> Rory). Stick insect. Roadrunner. Termite. Shrike. Frilled lizard.<br /> <br /> ...Those are the ones that jump to mind for brainstorming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's Rory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:48:12-07:00","id":853887,"title":"","content":"Rory Mercury is one of the major characters from Gate. She's a priestess of, I believe, a goddess of death, as well as a demigoddess - which, in this setting, means that she's scheduled to live a thousand years among mortals and then ascend. She's got about forty years left, and she's actually surprisingly sane for someone who's spent that long experiencing sexual stimulation whenever her body is used as a channel for a nearby departing soul to reach the afterlife - which is to say, we usually see her wantonly slaughtering people like bandits or opposing soldiers, rather than just whoever she can reach.<br /> <br /> The narration is also painfully clear that she's biologically frozen at around age twelve.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Neat character design, cool fighting style, <i>oh god, ICK</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T16:38:54-07:00","id":854245,"title":"","content":"I have yet to see an Armadillo Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T20:27:43-07:00","id":854342,"title":"","content":"I believe I saw mention of a pangolin-totem Lunar over on The Freedom Stone Forums, back when.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T00:44:55-07:00","id":854386,"title":"","content":"Armadillo-Lunar seems kind of obvious too.<br /> <br /> A good source of ideas is finding the mythic associations of animals in different cultures.<br /> <br /> For example, Chinese astrology is easy enough to research, and you can see the associations for each of the 12 animals. You probably think that something like a Snake is rather common, but what about a Chicken, Ox or Sheep?<br /> <br /> Or myths like the African trickster myths which generally feature animals like spiders or hares.<br /> <br /> Birds are good too, because a lot of birds have different associations. For example:<br /> <br /> A wise, bespectacled scholar - Owl<br /> A keen hunter - Eagle<br /> A shameless clotheshorse hot guy - Peacock (doesn't work for girls unfortunately)<br /> An infiltrator - Cuckoo<br /> A necromancer or war looter - Crow<br /> A sailor - Seagull<br /> A singer - Nightingale, Robin, tons of others<br /> A pacifist - Dove<br /> A thief - Magpie<br /> <br /> Etc. Perhaps not very exciting though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bron